			<div class="content" id="post-content-4468961">
									

<p>This, this is a masterful submission.</p>
<p>One just has to adore the finesse of your world-building; how seamlessly characters, places, events, and societies are interwoven with such seeming ease and familiarity that one can't help but buy in to every bit of it.</p>
<p>Not content to merely 'tell' in terms of creating this world, it's beautifully envisioned &#8212; the setting itself is meticulously crafted, the characters each bring a unique voice and perspective, the allure (pun intended?) of mystery all contribute to breathing life into this work. It bleeds creativity and imagination just as much as it [spoiler redacted].</p>
<p>It's a halmark of a good mystery that, in answering one question, many others may be raised, and some left hanging. This accomplishes just that (while also eliciting actual, physical chills &#8212; killer line to send off on). I'm certainly going to be revisiting this one in the future.</p>

							</div>

								
					
